---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="How we work" description="Where Broward Spotlight's information comes from, how paid placement works, and our review and corrections policies.">
  <div class="wrap stack-lg" style="max-width:760px">
    <header class="stack"><h1>How we work</h1><p>Broward Spotlight is an independent local directory. Our job is to put the facts about Broward businesses in one place and keep them honest.</p></header>
    <section class="stack" id="sources">
      <h2>Where the information comes from</h2>
      <p><strong>Public records.</strong> Restaurant, food truck and caterer listings, licenses and inspection results come from the Florida Department of Business and Professional Regulation's public data files. We import them every week and show inspection results in the state's own words. We are not affiliated with any government agency.</p>
      <p><strong>Business owners.</strong> Owners who claim their listing can add a description, hours, website and social links. Anything an owner writes is marked as written by the owner.</p>
      <p><strong>Customers.</strong> Reviews come from people who confirm their email and tell us they were real customers with no tie to the business.</p>
      <p><strong>Our research.</strong> Under "Around the web" we link to news stories and public discussions about a business, with a short summary in our own words. We don't copy other sites' content.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="stack" id="featured">
      <h2>Featured and Sponsored</h2>
      <p>Businesses can pay to appear in Featured spots at the top of city, category and search pages, to run a labeled ad, or to sponsor a Spotlight article. Paid placement is always labeled Featured, Sponsored or Advertisement.</p>
      <p>Paying never changes a state record, never hides or reorders reviews, and never buys an Owner verified badge. Verification is free for every business.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="stack" id="reviews">
      <h2>Review policy</h2>
      <p>We post every genuine review, positive or negative. Before a review goes live we check it for a short list of problems, and these are the only reasons we remove one:</p>
      <ul style="display:grid;gap:6px;padding-left:20px;margin:0">
        <li>It's spam, an ad, or about a different business.</li>
        <li>It contains threats, hate speech, or someone's private information.</li>
        <li>It was written by the owner, an employee, a relative, a competitor, or someone paid or rewarded for it.</li>
        <li>It's about an incident we have reason to believe didn't happen at this business.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Owners can reply publicly to any review. They can't remove or edit reviews, and we don't accept payment to do it.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="stack" id="corrections">
      <h2>Corrections and disputes</h2>
      <p>Every listing has a "Report a mistake" link. We check each report against the original source and fix our own errors quickly. State records are shown as the state publishes them; if a state record is wrong, the state has to correct it, and we pick up the fix on our next import.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
